  "description": "This cold, creamy Spanish tomato soup blends ripe tomatoes, bread, garlic, sherry vinegar, and olive oil into a quick and bright summer meal.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 35 min.\n\nOptional substitutions: baguette white bread → rustic white bread; Chopped jamón serrano → ibérico\n\nNotes: Jamón serrano, a dry-cured Spanish ham, is the more affordable and widely available option. Jamón ibérico, made from Iberian-breed pigs, has more intramuscular fat, giving it a richer flavor and texture that nearly melts on the tongue. For the most complex, nutty flavor, look for jamón ibérico de bellota, made from pigs that forage on acorns. Spanish specialty shops, well-stocked cheese counters, and online retailers often carry both serrano and ibérico; either works well here.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Leftovers can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 4 days.",
